      {
        "position": 1,
        "title": "Really helpful for arthritic dogs",
        "text": "I have several large dogs, two of which are older and suffer from arthritis, including a Chocolate Lab and an Australian Shepherd. Both of them have trouble getting into the back of my SUV and even up onto the couch. Picking them up can be a challenge: if you hold them to close to their hips, it can hurt them. So I was looking for something to help lift them up and I found this.The quality is superlative. It is incredibly well made, very heavily reinforced, and with a lovely soft furry lining on the inside to ensure the dog does not have any discomfort. I did find the straps to be a little bit long but they are adjustable.I tried it first with my Australian shepherd, who only weighs 50 lb. It was very easy to lift him up, just be careful when you position it that any . . . male parts . . . are not caught inside this harness, or it will hurt them. I was able to get my dog to put his front paws on the couch and then use this to lift him up and it was quick, easy, and painless.I then tried it with my chocolate lab, she was much less receptive to it. But once I let her sniff the harness and see that it would not hurt her, she let me wrap it around her and I was able to get her both onto the couch and into the back of my SUV with much less trouble than I normally experience.This is incredibly helpful and I highly recommend it if you have a large dog with mobility challenges that you need to help. The price is very fair for what you get, the quality is excellent, and it does what it is supposed to do effectively and efficiently.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "June 3, 2026",
        "author": "Amazon Customer",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AEWV4CHWFZ72AZIIR4ODWQKIFSOQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "images": [
          "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81jolgjMd6L.jpg",
          "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71ikNUaUayL.jpg",
          "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71y-5GElvDL.jpg"
        ],
        "product": {
          "size": "L"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 2,
        "title": "A winner for a senior dog",
        "text": "My 16 year old Aussie has arthritis in her back end and getting up forces all the weight on her front legs and is a struggle. As far as lifting her with the harness from a laying position, it takes some practice, as you have to get it under her which then makes her try and get up while you are trying to shove it under her. Once I got it under her and could grab the handles it made lifting her up less of a strain on her and me. This then gave her a chance to stabilize her balance.If she is already standing, putting the harness under her and using it to guide or stabilize her works pretty effortlessly. It also works ok to assist her up steps if she is able to do some of the forward motion.As for quality, this harness outweighs another I had tried as it has very nice soft fleece cushioning on the part surrounding her underbelly. The handles, material and stitching all seem durable. It even can be washed if it gets soiled.Other uses - dogs that have had surgery such as acl surgery would benefit from this to stabilize their surgery legs for standing and walking.Although I mention it takes some practice using it from a lay to stand position, I’m giving it 5 stars for its quality, softness and value. The handle is comfortable and there are side strap adjustments to accommodate your dog’s height.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "June 8, 2026",
        "author": "Zena",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AGIMZAC6C2PIR4VTDA3E6H6E3X2A?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "product": {
          "size": "M"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 3,
        "title": "Horrible Experience",
        "text": "Our senior tripod was ill and unable to stand. We bought this hoping we could help him. He ended up falling and busting his nose and the trauma with his illness was not good. That being said I can't recommend this product.",
        "rating": 1,
        "date": "June 11, 2026",
        "author": "Selina Hainley",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AF5LH5K5ZZFZCXJYWWQS2MVZ76VQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "verified_purchase": true,
        "product": {
          "size": "M"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 4,
        "title": "The Cadillac of support slings",
        "text": "This is an awesome product and honestly feels like the Cadillac of this type of support sling. The quality is excellent, the stitching feels strong, and the whole thing feels very well made.The inside is incredibly soft, which makes a big difference when using it with an older dog or a dog with mobility issues. It gives good support without feeling rough or uncomfortable against their belly. The handles are sturdy, and the adjustable straps make it easier to get a comfortable fit for both the dog and the person helping them.This is especially helpful for senior dogs, dogs with arthritis, back leg weakness, or pets recovering from surgery. It makes lifting, steadying, and helping them up steps or into a vehicle much easier and safer.Overall, I’m very impressed. It is soft, strong, supportive, and well worth having if your dog needs a little extra help getting around.",
