      {
        "position": 5,
        "title": "Sturdy sling",
        "text": "We've used a few slings lately for our boxer with degenerative myelopathy. There's a couple I really like and one that looks nice but ends up bunching up under her. This one is like the ones we like. It's stiffer but soft and stays flat under her. At first I didn't think I'd like the velcro attachment to connect the handles but I actually do. I just wish that part was softer instead of slick material, it'd be easier on hands. I put it in the washer (in a washer bag I already had) and it came out well, it is hanging to dry right now. A couple of the other types I have I threw in the washer but this one said hang dry. Overall though this sling is strong and sturdy for our 70 lb boxer (we ordered large), and I wouldn't hesitate to buy another.",
